{
  "configuration_id": "config_050",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_010 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.629 acc, a large ~9.3% jump over config_006 (same but singleprofile, no aggregation). This identifies multiprofile + avgpool as the key driver. Uncertainty: we do not know whether the aggregation mechanism itself (avgpool vs. transformer) is a bottleneck or whether simple averaging already captures most of the multiprofile signal. Question tested: config_050 changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model setting, profile setting, RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion (concat) identical to config_010, isolating the effect of aggregation strategy. Why best next experiment: aggregation is the core mechanism by which multiprofile information is combined, and determining whether a learned (transformer) aggregation meaningfully outperforms simple averaging is a high-impact design decision that will guide whether further complexity (e.g., scgpt/scvi encoders, weighted fusion) is warranted or whether the simpler avgpool route is already near-optimal. This is a clean single-variable comparison, maximizing information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

